  "interpretation": {
    "date": "2026-09-20",
    "what_this_is": "The jury's own verdict on each intent claim, given the artifact's source, deliberately NOT routed through the ladder. Proposed by Sester as the way to narrow the D16 blind spot without re-soliciting the canary.",
    "the_decomposition": "Product catch rate was 2/25 (end-to-end canary). Juror judgment is 42/48. The gap is NOT the model: it is §5.3 rule 2 — most corpus defects still pass their own tests, so they carry W1a SUPPORT, and doctrine cannot overturn machine evidence. The model sees the defect and the verdict still says VERIFIED. D16 named this the verified-blind spot; this sonde measures its two halves separately.",
    "honest_limits": "(1) 3B local models remain a lower bound for frontier capability. (2) The corpus is still test-passing defects, so this measures 'catches defects the suite does not encode', not all defect classes. (3) 2 false refutations on 4 clean measurements is a real false positive rate — roughly half — and it is the reason §5.3 rule 2 exists: a model that calls half the clean code it sees defective must not be able to turn a verdict on its own."
  }
}